        {
          "id": 1455111725,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I a bit in the lost after this change, macron is not really my thing :p \n\n```\n/wireshark/epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c: In function ‘check_ns_wraparound’:\n/wireshark/epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c:448:3: error: implicit declaration of function ‘_Generic’ [-Werror=implicit-function-declaration]\n   ws_safe_sub_jmp(&ns->nsecs, ns->nsecs, NS_PER_S, env);\n   ^\nIn file included from /wireshark/epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c:18:0:\n/wireshark/wsutil/safe-math.h:1010:5: error: expected expression before ‘char’\n     char: psnip_safe_char_##op, \\\n     ^\n/wireshark/wsutil/safe-math.h:1022:3: note: in expansion of macro ‘PSNIP_SAFE_C11_GENERIC_SELECTION’\n   PSNIP_SAFE_C11_GENERIC_SELECTION(res, op)(res, a, b)\n   ^\n/wireshark/wsutil/safe-math.h:1041:35: note: in expansion of macro ‘PSNIP_SAFE_C11_GENERIC_BINARY_OP’\n #define psnip_safe_sub(res, a, b) PSNIP_SAFE_C11_GENERIC_BINARY_OP(sub, res, a, b)\n                                   ^\n/wireshark/wsutil/safe-math.h:1052:13: note: in expansion of macro ‘psnip_safe_sub’\n         if(!psnip_safe_##op(res, a, b)) { \\\n             ^\n/wireshark/wsutil/safe-math.h:1058:41: note: in expansion of macro ‘ws_safe_op_jmp’\n #define ws_safe_sub_jmp(res, a, b, env) ws_safe_op_jmp(sub, res, a, b, env)\n                                         ^\n/wireshark/epan/ftypes/ftype-time.c:448:3: note: in expansion of macro ‘ws_safe_sub_jmp’\n   ws_safe_sub_jmp(&ns->nsecs, ns->nsecs, NS_PER_S, env);\n```\n\nCould this be unsupported behavior in GCC 4.8.5 ?",
